How not to drown in a box tsunami
Do you unwrap the gifts under the Christmas tree and suddenly you're at home covered with boxes and fillings?
This "waste" is again used by e-shops that lack packaging materials.
Therefore, a map of the shops was created, which will welcome your used boxes.
And not just at Christmas.
All packaging materials are designed to withstand repeated handling.
That's why it's a shame to treat them as disposable waste.
Anyone can, by agreement, bring cardboard boxes, plastic or paper fillings to the participating shop (the KAMSNIM.cz project map contains almost 150 of them).
In doing so, it will support small businesses, reduce the amount of waste generated, and also avoid overcrowded blue containers.
The shops themselves welcome packaging, which is currently scarce on the market and also saved money, as packaging carton has increased by 50% over the last period.
Moreover, in the eyes of eco-minded customers, this strengthens my brand.
One of such stores is TIERRA VERDE, a manufacturer of eco drugstores and eco cosmetics.
The boxes and filling material are brought to us by individuals who accumulate at home, but we also hear from companies with whom we have arranged regular collections of deferred cartons.
We will use everything when packing shipments from our e-shop.
Thanks to individuals and companies together, we create a more considerate world.
Our wish is to preserve the resources and beauty of nature to future generations, says Petra Lopušníková from Tierra.
However, the application www.KAMSNIM.cz shows not only sampling points for packaging material.
It serves as a search engine if you need to get rid of anything (where to take the sorted waste from the home, where to hand over expired medicines, tires, retired electro, batteries, light sources, high-volume waste, etc.).
Thus, all garbage can end up in the right place, in addition, reusable things will find their second home.
In total, the map of the project contains more than 100 000 such places.
“Gradually, collection yards, re-use centers, textile containers, food banks, charity shops, SWAPs and other places that help to find use for things that would otherwise unnecessarily become waste,” adds Miroslav Kubásek, one of the authors of the application from the Uclime Česko association.
