Bethlehem flame is in the Czech Republic, scouts took it from Austria
Břeclav – The flame ignited in Bethlehem, where Jesus Christ was born according to Christian tradition, is in the Czech Republic.
Scouts did not even go to Vienna for him this time due to the coronavirus pandemic, in the morning they took it from their Austrian colleagues at the Reintal-Břeclav border crossing.
It was also taken over at the border last year.
Bethlehem Light is a beautiful Christmas tradition, which we participate with the squad every year, I look forward to it very much.
It is an honor for me to have been chosen, scout Amálie Alarmová told reporters.
While last year's handover took place at the Mikulov-Drasenhofen border crossing, directly on the border bridge, now at the Reintal-Břeclav crossing in the parking lot.
However, scouts usually travel by train to Vienna.
Nothing has changed about the distribution of the flame in the Czech Republic.
With Bethlehem light, scouts traditionally took a train first to Brno, where it will be handed over to the diocesan bishop Vojtěch Cikrlem.
Scout couriers will take care of the subsequent distribution of the light on Saturday, December 18, who will travel by selected express trains and passenger trains.
Local scouts or volunteers will take the light from them, who will then continue to spread flames around the Czech Republic and where the tracks do not lead.
Even this year, scouts must comply with current measures against the spread of coronavirus.
It’s the same as last year.
We give recommendations to both those courier teams and the organizers of local events to wear masks, try to observe spacings, there were as few of them as possible, do not sing colleagues, simply behave in such a way as safe as possible, Zuzana Hrbková, spokeswoman for the event of nativity light, described.
The tradition of Bethlehem light, which travels through Europe, was born in 1986 in Austria.
The goal is to spread the idea of peace, friendship and peace at the same time with the flame.
Bethlehem’s light is a symbol of hope for believers, a light that overcomes darkness.
Scouts and scouts have been taking care of its spread in the Czech Republic for more than 30 years.
The event stands on hundreds of volunteers, the flame is also a symbol of selflessness and human reciprocity.
All news, including a list of places where people can come for flames, can be found on the website www.betlemskesvetlo.cz.
