§ 152 Spread of contagious human disease
(1) Whoever intentionally causes or increases the risk of the introduction or spread of contagious disease in humans shall be punished by imprisonment for six months to three years, by prohibition of activity or forfeiture of things.
(2) By imprisonment for two years to eight years, the offender will be punished,
(c) if such an act violates an important obligation arising from his employment, profession, position or function or imposed on him under the law; or
(d) if such an act causes serious injury to health.
(3) By imprisonment for three years to ten years, the offender shall be punished if, by the act referred to in paragraph 1, he causes serious injury to the health of at least two persons or death.
(4) By imprisonment for five to twelve years, the offender shall be punished if, by the act referred to in paragraph 1, causes the death of at least two persons.
