Vicki Holland from Britain tortured cosman Milly's monkey
Horrifying footage shows the moment when the terrified monkey crouched in the toilet bowl before her heartless owner flushed her and laughed at her.
Holland also fetched sausages, kebabs and burgers, regardless of her actual nutritional needs.
Gwent magistrates' court has now banned her from raising animals for life, The Sun newspaper reported.
Rehabilitation experts who take care of Milly after her abuse said they had never seen such a frightened cosman.
Milly has spent almost two years rehabilitating Monkey Workers in Dorset and is now playing happily again with another rescued ape called Moon.
The four-time mother pleaded guilty to two allegations of inflicting unnecessary suffering on a protected animal.
A twelve-week prison sentence was imposed at the Gwent magistrate's court with a suspended sentence of one year.
Hollandová was also sentenced to 120 hours of unpaid work, was given a lifetime ban on animal husbandry and has to pay 12 000 crowns of court costs.
The leader of the Small Monkeys team who rehabilitated the abused animal, Steph Sawyer, said: "Milly is fine, but the rehabilitation will continue even further."
Milly took time to get used to people again.
She crouched and hid from everyone she met, and any loud sound or sudden movement made her scream.
The monkey refused to eat for a long time.
Even now that she's settled down and she's happy with the male, the sight of new people can still create panic.
Mental scars from abuse will accompany her forever, Sawyer adds.
