More than 60 percent of voters came to Saturday's elections to the councils of four municipalities
On Saturday, new councils elected people in the villages of Komňa in Uherskohradiště region, Lužice in the Mostecko region, Nová Ves in the Liberec region and in Rovná na Pelhřimov region.
The number of representatives in these municipalities fell below the stipulated number or the elected municipalities collapsed.
There were a total of 28 candidates on Saturday.
The average age of newly elected representatives is 46.7 years.
The oldest of them is 69, the youngest 33 years old.
The processing of the results of Saturday's elections symbolically concludes a rather challenging but successful year for us.
A total of four new or repeated elections to municipal councils and, above all, high-profile elections to the Chamber of Deputies took place, said Vice-President Eva Krumpová.
She recalled that because of the covid-19 outbreak, the election was more demanding on both equipment and personnel security.
Saturday's election was won by the Association of Independent Candidates, which received 27.76 percent of the vote and two seats in the seven-member council.
The STAN candidate received 24.84 percent of the vote, which also means winning two seats.
Two seats in the council were also won by Citizens for Komňa, 18.52 percent of the electorate gave them their vote.
Jana Křižková, the current mayor of the municipality, who is a member of the Privateers, has also reclaimed them.
For one mandate in the council, Comenians – independent candidates – have achieved.
75.48 percent of eligible voters came to the polls.
In the village of Rovná in the Pelhřimov region, the association Pro Rovnou won.
It won 50.50 percent of the vote, meaning four seats out of seven.
Two representatives from the Association of Independent Candidates 1 and one from the Association of Independent Candidates 2 came to the municipal council.
Voter turnout was 93.62 percent.
Repeated elections in Lusatia in the Most region were won again by the Lusatian and Svinčice Association led by Mayor Jindřich John.
It won 56.73 percent of the vote and, as in 2018, has four seats in the seven-member council.
The second ended with the municipality's candidate for the people, which 43.27 percent of the electorate gave the vote, so she will have three representatives in the council.
76.7 percent of voters came to the polls.
The elections in Nová Ves in the Liberec region were won by independent candidates of Hope for Nová Ves in front of the ANO Movement.
59.88 percent of voters voted for the association of independent candidates, gaining four seats in the seven-member municipal council.
ANO received 40.12 percent of the vote and strengthened against regular elections in 2018, won a mandate more and has three.
Voter turnout was 42.9 percent of voters.
On Monday, the State Electoral Commission will discuss the election results.
It will then be published in the Collection of Laws.
