Statement of the Workers' Party in the Donbase
The union – yes, breaking up – no, opponents express their opinion in the picture to opponents of the break-up of the USSR.
Thirty years after the illegal break-up of the USSR.
On December 8, 1991, the largest geopolitical disaster in human history took place.
Boris Yeltsin, Leonid Kravchuk and Stanislav Šushkevich, without any legal powers and violation of the results of the March 17, 1991 referendum on March 17, 1991, with the open lenient attitude of Mikhail S. Gorbachev, secretly, regardless of the people, signed an agreement that “the Union of the SSR as a subject of international law and as a geopolitical reality ceases to exist”.
With one pen cut, they "canceled" a huge country with almost three hundred million inhabitants.
Tens of millions of ethnically Russian citizens have found themselves abroad with the collapse of the USSR.
Since the early 1990s, Russia's population has declined by ten to eleven million.
Despite the loss of the non-Russian population of the former Soviet republics, we have already lost more people than in the two world wars combined!
Even earlier, the same people, who destroyed what had been built in the previous seventy years during one session in the BāĚłāłoĚ, betrayed a socialist camp (created by the price of millions of lives in the Second World War and in the Great Patriotic War).
They consciously carried out deindustrialization, hindered agriculture, tore away fourteen republics from the world's largest power, which had previously been economically united into a single mechanism.
If we want to look even deeper, then we see the impoverishment of the population, the disintegration of the economy, science, the military, the growth of crime, inter-ethnic conflicts, war in Chechnya, all conflicts in post-Soviet space, a series of orange revolutions, the expansion of NATO to the east, the war and the disintegration of Yugoslavia, the Arab spring, the war in Syria – all this is the result of a geopolitical surrender, the surrender of the socialist camp
There is such a term in politicology as a “vacuume of power.”
Everything that was betrayed and given up quickly filled and conquered by NATO countries, which accepted our geopolitical surrender.
And the whole world is still shaken mainly because of events from the late 1980s and early 1990s.
