Skiers went to the mountains this weekend, waiting for plenty of snow and nice weather
Mountain resorts in the Czech Republic experienced this weekend's first major onslaught of those interested in skiing.
After heavy snowfall at the end of the working week, there is no shortage of snow, and some ski resorts have started operations.
Downhill skiers have also not been deterred by the obligation to prove themselves with a Covid certificate for lifts.
While lifters don't complain about customer disinterest, some ski equipment rental companies are reporting weaker demand for their services than before the outbreak.
Thousands of people in the Liberec Region went to the cross-country trails and the slopes at the weekend.
Skiers enjoyed the weather, which today offered the sun and excellent snow conditions.
“We are satisfied, the opening weekend really came out from that Friday evening skiing, when we had the first skiers on the hill,” Jakub Hanuš, the director of the Ještěd Sports Complex, praised his interest.
Hundreds of people went for the first weekend skiing in the new season also to Jeseníky.
They were open, for example, Ski Arena Karlov or a resort in Branná in the Šumperk region.
Weekend attendances were very decent, an estimated 400 people came on Saturday and today.
The conditions are cool.
Today the sun was shining, it was around minus three degrees, so the perfect did not spare praise the representative of the ski resort in Branná Rostislav Procházka.
Ski resort operators can sell ski passes only to people who are vaccinated or who are within the deadline after experiencing covid-19.
With exceptions, people are prepared for this and are proving themselves with the necessary documents, René Hroneš from Špindlerův Mlyn ski center told ČTK.
"We've only detected units of incidents," he added.
Lower interest than before the pandemic is reported by some ski equipment rentals and stores.
Fortunately, there is an interest in renting skis.
It's not like in previous years, but there are still plenty of customers, said Alexandra Bokišová from Skiopava's Opava store.
It expects a bigger onslaught during ski courses.
David Šinták, managing director of Snowbear in Hradec Králové, also feels that due to COVID there is no such interest in renting ski equipment as before.
By this time before the pandemic, we've almost been lendered.
Compared to the period before the pandemic, we are at about 50 percent, Šinták told ČTK.
According to him, people were lazy with the pandemic and learned how to sit at home.
On the contrary, a large demand is recorded by a rental company in the Novako area on Boží Dar.
They started renting skis there a week ago, and those interested already have to order them in advance.
“We’re starting to rent this weekend, but people have already called in advance, so we expect a lot of interest, just like last year,” said Pavlína Nováková, the operator of the complex.
According to her, the interest comparable to the period before the epidemic is also in the ski school.
