New timetables have been in force in Prague since Sunday, they will mainly affect suburban connections
Passengers in Prague Integrated Transport (PID) are waiting for several changes from Sunday, mainly related to suburban connections.
New lines were created, some have changed the route, and others have disappeared.
Mladoboleslavsko is newly involved in the integrated system.
In the capital since Sunday, speedsters from České Budějovice have been stopping at Zahradní Město station.
In suburban train transport, S7 trains will depart on the route from Beroun to Český Brod through the Prague Central Station.
In the recently commissioned Prague-Garden City station, the R17 expressway from České Budějovice and Benešov will be newly stopped.
PID will now spread to other areas.
Among other things, there will be buses to Světlá nad Sázavou, Blatna u Jesenice, Staré Splavy and Turnov.
Buses will be included in the Mladá Boleslav region, including routes with an overlap to the Liberec and Hradec Králové regions.
77 lines will be abolished during integration, 37 new lines will be introduced and traffic will be adjusted on the 12.
A new bus line 405, which will go all the way to Žatec, will depart from Zličín in Prague.
There was also a new direct connection Prague – Kralovice near Rakovník, which replaces the cancelled train line S53.
It will be strengthened in the morning rush hour and on the weekend connections from Prague to Rakovník, when the express line number 404 will newly depart.
Now lines 400 and 410 running to the Liberec region are included in the PID system.
They run from Střížkov metro station, not from Nádraží Holešovice station.
The backbone line 400 goes through Mělník, Duba and Česká Lípa to Nový Bor and the selected connections continue to Rumburk or Cvikova.
Complementary line 410 goes through Mělník and Dubou to Doks, Mimoň and Jablonné in Podještědí.
On the contrary, the operation on dozens of Central Bohemian local lines, among others to Mochov, Dobříš or Rožmitál pod Třemšínem, is cancelled or limited.
All trains with departure from Prague at 02:30 are canceled.
Due to the modernization of the railway, long-term restrictions continue on the lines of Prague – Beroun, Prague – Lysá nad Labem and around Kolín.
Changes await passengers in other places, too.
Buses replace some cancelled railway lines or expand the section on line 420 from Dobříš with connection from Prague, where it is possible to use PID tickets up to Milevsko.
The routes of lines 540 to 543 in Nymburk have undergone a change, and the routes of some buses on the border of Central Bohemia and Hořovice in the Pilsen region have been modified.
