There are more types of bosses.
For example, a game like Dark Souls, etc. has bosses a few, right, and so "boss" is something like a gentleman / ruler of a given level, and then there's the final boss...
In many games there are hidden bosses (super boss, hidden boss) who do not need to beat the game or the level is complete, but they are often even stronger than the standard boss.
Then there are games like Half-Life, where there are bosses, but the player doesn’t directly compete with them (Tentacle, Gargantua), and can they be called that at all?
And then they're mini bosses.
On a flat-rate one-word way to translate the boss is simply not possible, Czech and other languages do not solve it in any way (it is interesting only Catalan, which translates the boss as the final opponent).
It is, in short, for a story or game generally significant, computer-dominated, adversary stronger than all the previous ones and guarding the completion of some level or task.
