Pre-Christmas Czech Republic is terrorized by Agent Tesla.
While data in October indicated a slight decline in attack campaigns, last month, with the end of the year approaching, attacks intensified significantly.
We saw a big campaign in connection with Agent Tesla on November 18.
The attacks are focused on the Czech Republic.
For the time being, the striker's strategy remains the same.
An infected attachment in an e-mail is supposed to attract attention in the user with a name that refers to payments and financial transactions.
While last month the dangerous attachment in the name had the word invoice, this time it was labeled as a copy of the receipt correction for 11.2021...exe," Martin Jirkal from Esetu said in a statement.
Spyware includes features that scan Internet browsers and other programs, such as Microsoft Outlook, Mozilla Thunderbird or Yandex email clients.
The malicious code actively searches for stored credentials, which it then sends to attackers.
The last strong campaign took place in the Czech Republic at the turn of August and September, and with the upcoming holidays and the end of the year, the activity of attackers grows again.
Spyware Formbook also remained active in November.
Unlike Agent Tesla, in this case, attackers do not specifically target the Czech Republic, and security specialists intercepted rather campaigns with a global reach in November.
Compared to the October data, Formbook weakened slightly in November, but continues to be behind almost a fifth of all detections.
The attacks took place continuously throughout the month with increased activity on 3, 10 and 15 November.
Formbook most often included an attachment with the extension .exe, which was called REQUEST FOR SPECIFICATION.
However, the name of the receipt continues to appear.
The appendix in Czech can then be much more dangerous for the Czech user.
A significant decrease and suppression of activity is recorded by security analysts at the Fareit program, which accounted for 1.6 percent of the attacks and has not had a major attack campaign in the Czech Republic for the last few months.
