End of stalemate, Bulgaria has a new prime minister proclaiming change
Bulgarian President Rumen Radev has commissioned the formation of a new government of Kiril Petkov from the anti-corruption movement We continue to change, which won the November elections.
This has already managed to form a government of a broad coalition, which should take office within a few days.
The country's political crisis has been going on since April, when the past government, under the weight of anti-corruption protests, lost elections.
However, victorious parties proclaiming the fight against bribery and abuse of power were unable to agree, so two more early elections followed.
