There were growing fears in Britain this weekend about the fate of a 32-year-old Czech woman who has been searched by London police for several days.
Petra Srncova was last seen two weeks ago when she went home from work to the south of the British metropolis.
In addition to the police, information about a children's hospital worker is being called upon by her current employer or an MP representing part of London where she lived.
“Petra’s disappearance doesn’t resemble her behavior at all and we’re starting to be very worried about her,” Lucy O’Connor said in Saturday’s video.
“Her family in the Czech Republic is also very worried about her and she just wants to know where she is,” she continued.
According to her, on Sunday, November 28, around 19:45 she left work and headed home to Camberwell district.
She was reportedly seen on the bus about half an hour later.
Her disappearance was reported on December 3 by one of her co-workers
According to British media, Srncova worked as an "assistant of nurses" at Evelina London Children's Hospital, which belongs to Guy's and St Thomas' hospital.
"We are extremely concerned about our dear colleague Petra, who is missing," a group of medical facilities said in a Twitter post.
"We'd like to encourage anyone who could have any information that might help her find to contact the police," the statement continued.
